            "question": "Find the area of a quadrilateral ABCD in which AB=3cm, BC=4cm, CD=4cm, DA=5cm and AC=5cm.",
            "finalAnswer": "15.16 cm² (approx)",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "$\\\\triangle ABC$ is right-angled ($3^2+4^2=5^2$). Area1 = $1/2 \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6$ cm².",
                "$\\\\triangle ADC$ has sides 5, 4, 5. $s = (5+5+4)/2 = 7$. Area2 = $\\\\sqrt{7(2)(2)(3)} = \\\\sqrt{84} \\approx 9.16$ cm².",
                "Total Area = $6 + 9.16 = 15.16$ cm²."
            ]
        },
